`get_sizes_advanced` starts with the full `(711, 1009)` area and offsets `(17, 29)`, then repeatedly calls `_get_row_or_col` for the remaining windows. `calc` chooses the grid whose per-tile aspect ratio is closest to `0.63`, so the sequence is: 13 windows as a `ROWCOL` strip of 4 across the top; then 9 windows as a `COLROW` strip of 4 down the left; then 6 windows as a `ROWCOL` strip of 3 across the top of the remaining area; then 3 windows as a final `ROWCOL` strip of 3. `_get_row_or_col` uses integer division for base sizes and gives the last tile in the strip the leftover width or height, which yields the exact rectangles below.

